/T (It's actually surprising how such a concept actually helps in constructing the prototype, so we made sure that almost no energy is wasted because of the wrong choice of materials and their properties. Three properties adopted: - First: plasticity. This one is present in the filament used for printing the prototype, it can be pulled and shaped however we want without breaking down, which'll serve not collapsing while we are testing the prototype. Second: Strength. After printing the turbine, it looked soft \(driving us for the third property\) and delicate, but when applying vertical and horizontal pressure on it, we discovered that the turbine is actually stiff, holding up to 20 kilograms without breaking down, which means it can bear the ultimate- )
/E (It's actually surprising how such a concept actually helps in constructing the prototype, so we made sure that almost no energy is wasted because of the wrong choice of materials and their properties. Three properties adopted: - First: plasticity. This one is present in the filament used for printing the prototype, it can be pulled and shaped however we want without breaking down, which'll serve not collapsing while we are testing the prototype. Second: Strength. After printing the turbine, it looked soft \(driving us for the third property\) and delicate, but when applying vertical and horizontal pressure on it, we discovered that the turbine is actually stiff, holding up to 20 kilograms without breaking down, which means it can bear the ultimate- )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
