/E (high speeds of the winds caused by metro train the turbine will be applied in. Third: Texture. as mentioned before, the filament printed is pretty soft, which means there won't be energy wasted in friction of the rough surface, neither would it be harder to deal with when applying to the other components, to not scratch them. Two properties rejected: First: Elasticity. Elasticity means the material comes to its original shape after deforming, which we absolutely don't need for using filament, because it won't be shaped as the hybrid turbine we need. Second: Bounce. this concept of a property means how the material bounce on ground when thrown of a given height. We won't be throwing our turbine anyway, so we won't have advantage of using it.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
